NuVTNCN1NLVWthbWt4X2RUUg?oc=5","date":"2026-10-22","zh":"富國銀行 (NYSE:WFC.PRD) 股票預測和分析師預測"},{"title":"SpaceX (NASDAQ:SPCX) Stock Gets Price Target Increase from Wells Fargo & Company","src":"MarketBeat","url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","date":"2026-10-21","zh":"富國銀行提高 SpaceX （納斯達克股票代碼：SPCX）股票目標價格"}],"themes":[{"name":"分析師評等","count":5},{"name":"財報","count":2},{"name":"股票回購/股利","count":2},{"name":"AI 人工智慧","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-24","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/72971/000007297126000133/wfc-20251231_d2.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Wells Fargo & Company is a corporation organized under the laws of Delaware and a financial holding company and a bank holding company registered under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956, as amended (BHC Act). Its principal business is to act as a holding company for its subsidiaries. References in this report to \"the Parent\" mean the holding company. References to \"we,\" \"our,\" \"us\" or \"the Company\" mean the holding company and its subsidiaries that are consolidated for financial reporting purposes.","zh":"Wells Fargo & Company 是一家根据特拉华州法律组建的公司，也是根据 1956 年《银行控股公司法》（经修订）（BHC 法）注册的金融控股公司和银行控股公司。其主要業務為其附屬公司的控股公司。本報告中提及的「母公司」是指控股公司。提及的「我們」、「我們的」或「本公司」是指出於財務報告目的而合併的控股公司及其子公司。"},{"en":"At December 31, 2025, we had assets of approximately $2.1 trillion, loans of $986.2 billion, deposits of $1.4 trillion and stockholders' equity of $181.1 billion. Based on assets, we were the fourth largest bank holding company in the United States. At December 31, 2025, Wells Fargo Bank, N.A. (the Bank) was the Company's principal subsidiary with assets of $1.8 trillion, or 85% of the Company's assets.","zh":"截至2025年12月31日，我们的资产约为2.1万亿美元，贷款为9862亿美元，存款为1.4万亿美元，股东权益为1811亿美元。以資產計算，我們是美國第四大銀行控股公司。截至2025年12月31日，Wells Fargo Bank, N.A.（以下简称“银行”）是公司的主要子公司，资产达1.8万亿美元，占公司资产的85%。"},{"en":"Form 10-Q, current reports on Form 8-K, and amendments to those reports, are available for free at www.wellsfargo.com/about/investor-relations/filings as soon as reasonably practicable after they are electronically filed with or furnished to the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC). They are also available for free on the SEC's website at www.sec.gov1.","zh":"表 10-Q、表 8-K 中的最新报告以及这些报告的修订版以电子方式提交给美国证券交易委员会 (SEC) 后，可在合理可行的情况下尽快免费访问 www.wellsfargo.com/about/investor-relations/filings。它們也可在 SEC 網站 www.sec.gov1 上免費取得。"}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"The financial services industry is highly competitive. Our subsidiaries compete with financial services providers such as banks, savings and loan associations, credit unions, finance companies, mortgage banking companies, insurance companies, investment banks, investment advisory firms, and mutual fund companies. They also face increased competition from nonbank institutions such as investment managers, brokerage houses, private equity and private credit firms, and financial technology companies, as well as from financial services subsidiaries of commercial and manufacturing companies. Many of these competitors enjoy fewer regulatory constraints and some may have lower cost structures.","zh":"金融服務業競爭激烈。我们的子公司与银行、储蓄和贷款协会、信用合作社、财务公司、抵押银行公司、保险公司、投资银行、投资咨询公司和共同基金公司等金融服务提供商竞争。它们还面临来自投资管理公司、经纪公司、私募股权和私人信贷公司、金融科技公司等非银行机构以及商业和制造公司的金融服务子公司的日益激烈的竞争。許多競爭對手的監管限制較少，有些競爭對手的成本結構可能較低。"},{"en":"Securities firms and insurance companies that elect to become financial holding companies may acquire banks and other financial institutions. Combinations of this type could significantly change the competitive environment in which we conduct business. The financial services industry is also becoming more competitive as further technological advances and the expansion of a digital economy have enabled non-depository institutions to offer products and services traditionally offered by banks and have enabled financial institutions, technology companies, and others to deliver electronic and internet-based financial solutions, including electronic securities trading, lending, savings, and payment solutions. Additionally, digital assets and alternative payment methods, such as cryptocurrencies, stablecoins, and tokens, as well as distributed ledger-based payment, clearing, and settlement proc","zh":"證券公司、保險公司選擇成為金融控股公司，可以收購銀行等金融機構。這種類型的組合可能會顯著改變我們開展業務的競爭環境。随着技术的进一步进步和数字经济的扩张，非存款机构能够提供传统上由银行提供的产品和服务，并使金融机构、科技公司和其他机构能够提供电子和基于互联网的金融解决方案，包括电子证券交易、借贷、储蓄和支付解决方案，金融服务业的竞争也变得更加激烈。此外，数字资产和替代支付方式，例如加密货币、稳定币和代币，以及基于分布式账本的支付、清算和结算流程"}],"segments":{},"peers":["BAC","C","JPM","GS","MS"]}}